<rml>
<head>
	<title>Repeating decorators</title>
	<meta name="folio-size" content="768x448"/>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="/folio/folio.rcss"/>
	<style>
		/* The `repeat` family lets the sampler do the tiling: RmlUi draws one quad whose texture
		   coordinates run to the tile count, rather than a quad per tile. That needs wrap
		   sampling, and the engine reaches it through a batch draw flag rather than the texture's
		   own address mode - so this document is the case that catches it going missing.

		   Read it as a grid. The tile is a white-and-blue frame with a yellow corner block and a
		   red diagonal, all asymmetric on purpose: wrapped, every cell looks like every other
		   cell. Clamped, the first cell is right and the rest of the element is its edge row
		   stretched, which is a smear rather than an error.

		   Also here because `repeat` is the only fit mode that cannot name a sprite. RmlUi refuses
		   it in both renderers, with a warning, since a sub-rectangle of an atlas has nothing to
		   wrap against - so the source is a file. */
		body
		{
			font-family: Inter;
			font-size: 13dp;
			color: #7b8494;
			background-color: #0d1015;
			width: 100%;
			height: 100%;
			padding: 24dp;
			box-sizing: border-box;
			display: flex;
			flex-wrap: wrap;
		}

		.cell { width: 224dp; margin: 0 20dp 20dp 0; }
		.label { margin-bottom: 6dp; }
		.box { height: 128dp; }

		.both { decorator: image(/folio/examples/tile_check.png repeat); }
		.across { decorator: image(/folio/examples/tile_check.png repeat-x); }
		.down { decorator: image(/folio/examples/tile_check.png repeat-y); }

		/* Under a filter the geometry goes through a layer rather than straight to Slate, which is
		   a second sampler and the one that has been wrong on its own. */
		.layered { decorator: image(/folio/examples/tile_check.png repeat); filter: brightness(1.4); }

		/* Half a tile wide, so the coordinates stay inside the unit square and wrapping and
		   clamping agree. It has to keep looking like a plain stretched tile. */
		.sub { width: 32dp; height: 32dp; decorator: image(/folio/examples/tile_check.png repeat); }
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<div class="cell">
		<div class="label">repeat</div>
		<div class="box both"/>
	</div>
	<div class="cell">
		<div class="label">repeat-x</div>
		<div class="box across"/>
	</div>
	<div class="cell">
		<div class="label">repeat-y</div>
		<div class="box down"/>
	</div>
	<div class="cell">
		<div class="label">repeat, through a layer</div>
		<div class="box layered"/>
	</div>
	<div class="cell">
		<div class="label">smaller than one tile</div>
		<div class="sub"/>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
